; The protocol core: no I/O, no scheduler, no clock, no ambient randomness, no
; unix. Every operation that needs entropy takes an Mpc.Rand.t; every operation
; that needs time takes a Timeout input the driver injects. That is what lets
; the same code drive a Unix process, a Solo5 unikernel, and a deterministic
; in-memory simulator, and it is why mirage-crypto-rng is a test dependency
; only. Deliberately free of zarith: nothing here needs a bignum.

(library
 (name mpc)
 (public_name mpc)
 (modules_without_implementation group)
 (libraries digestif eqaf))
